\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7}{\ignorespaces Trajectory-linked camera views from the accepted corrected \texttt  {validation\_002} task. Views 1--5 link locally to the radial--cross-track ($x$--$z$) projection, and views 6--10 link to the along-track--cross-track ($y$--$z$) projection; hollow gray markers retain the other observations as context. Inset labels give mission time and cumulative coverage. Dashed gray and solid blue denote planned and executed paths, and the star is the initial state. Apparent overlap in either projection does not imply contact: the annotated clearances and collision decision use the full 3-D transformed mesh and swept path. Gazebo rendered the views, while ROS HCW dynamics propagated state; coverage came from frozen geometric visibility masks, not image pixels.}}{13}{figure.90}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:ros-key-camera-views}{{7}{13}{Trajectory-linked camera views from the accepted corrected \texttt {validation\_002} task. Views 1--5 link locally to the radial--cross-track ($x$--$z$) projection, and views 6--10 link to the along-track--cross-track ($y$--$z$) projection; hollow gray markers retain the other observations as context. Inset labels give mission time and cumulative coverage. Dashed gray and solid blue denote planned and executed paths, and the star is the initial state. Apparent overlap in either projection does not imply contact: the annotated clearances and collision decision use the full 3-D transformed mesh and swept path. Gazebo rendered the views, while ROS HCW dynamics propagated state; coverage came from frozen geometric visibility masks, not image pixels}{figure.90}{}}
